    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Junior Caminero**, who earns our premier efficiency score of 77.68. His matchup against Mason Barnett is highly favorable; a combination of a hitter-friendly environment and optimal #3-hole placement makes him our most bankable asset. Close behind him, **Yordan Alvarez** (71.23) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (69.59) are locked into high-leverage spots despite the lack of a specific opposing starter, with the former benefiting from elite power metrics and favorable wind conditions, and the latter providing essential speed in our pursuit of stolen bases. We are particularly bullish on **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) and **Christian Yelich** (65.65), both of whom benefit from significant platoon advantages against Tomoyuki Sugano and Walker Buehler, respectively, elevating their projected output well above their base expectations.\n\nWhile the top of the order is solidified, we are closely monitoring the bottom of the lineup, where **Gary Sanchez** and **Dillon Dingler** (scoring 49.24 and 48.12) remain in marginal territory due to their position in the order and the quality of their opposition. The most difficult personnel decision involved **Carson Benge** (50.14), who sits just outside the starting nine; while his SP skill adjustment against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez was notable, his platoon disadvantage as a left-handed hitter facing a left-handed pitcher ultimately prompted the optimizer to favor the higher-upside profiles of our starting outfielders. We advise caution regarding **Trea Turner** (65.12); while his raw score is strong, his value is predicated heavily on aggressive base running against Andre Pallante. Should the official lineups reveal **Trea Turner** or any other core starter dropped from their projected spots, we may see further volatility in our daily efficiency rankings.",
